WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:09.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:14.968
-I'm a little irked,
and I'll get to why.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:20.767
I'm not gonna let it sully
the whole proceedings.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:26.434
But I'm starting from irked.

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:29.334
It said that Joe Biden got rid
of Daylight Savings Time.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:34.367
Not true. The Senate voted
to make it permanent.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.501
The House has yet to vote on it.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:42.968
There was a vote scheduled
in March, at 1:00 p.m.

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:44.567
Everyone showed up at 2:00.

00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:46.567
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:55.300
I said the "Star Trek" character
Scotty

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:58.734
was not in
"The Next Generation."

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.834
And if you're wondering

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:04.133
why your Internet was slow
last Friday,

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:06.234
I think it's
'cause all the tubes were jammed

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.000
with jackals telling me,

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.067
"Scotty did in fact appear
in a 'TNG' episode, 'Relics.'"

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:15.167
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:21.267
And this is interesting.

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:23.300
[ Sighs ]
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:29.300
[ Yawning ] Scotty survived
for decades in a derelict ship.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.300
[ Snores ]

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.300
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.767
Ooh!

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.234
We talked about
the Mandela Effect.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:43.734
The reason we were talking
about Scott in the first place

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:46.200
is in Star Trek, they never
said, "Beam me up, Scotty."

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.567
You know what's really nice?

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:51.567
Is how it's a beautiful shadow,
the way it's falling.

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:55.267
It's just making my head look
super symmetrical.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:57.267
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:01.868
No one ever said,
"Beat me up, Scotty."

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:06.567
In the "Sherlock Holmes" book
by Sir --

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:12.067
You always leave that part out.
Sir Arthur Conan Doyle --

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:15.100
Sherlock Holmes never said,
"Elementary, my dear Watson."

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:19.033
I guess the actual line

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:20.467
was Watson would say
some lines like,

00:02:20.467 --> 00:02:22.267
"Holmes, how did you deduce?"

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:24.634
And he'd go,
"I used my [bleep] brain, dude."

00:02:24.634 --> 00:02:27.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:33.400
You know, if I could go back
in time and meet anyone --

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.968
people say
if you could have dinner

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:37.567
with anyone, living or dead --

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:40.434
I think I'd most want to meet
the first guy

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:43.801
who said, "No [bleep] Sherlock,"
as a joke.

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:47.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.801
It must have been amazing...

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:50.801
the first time.

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:52.100
Obviously, it gets old,

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:56.200
but the first time someone said,
"No [bleep] Sherlock."

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.067
First Sherlock Holmes
was like 1887,

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:01.501
so what do we think -- 40 years?

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:02.667
40 years, I would imagine,

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:06.901
till the first time
someone made the joke.

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:10.367
[ Light laughter ]
I don't know.

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:14.834
Maybe it's like
after the Hindenberg,

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:16.067
they're talking about it,
and someone says,

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.234
"I think this is gonna be
a real blow

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:22.234
to zeppelin commercial travel."

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:25.534
"No [bleep] --"
Just would have been amazing.

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:27.534
Milli Vanilli --

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:29.801
I said they were caught
when their song skipped

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:34.234
on the "you"
in "Girl You Know It's True."

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:35.234
It was on the "Girl, you know."

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:36.367
It was right out of the --

00:03:36.367 --> 00:03:39.901
I guess that was where they knew
the game was up.

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:42.267
I also said that Shoemaker
was a fan of Milli Vanilli,

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:46.300
and he pretty angrily
correcting me on that,

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.801
so I'm sorry.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:50.033
According to him,
fans of Milli Vanilli

00:03:50.033 --> 00:03:51.767
are known as Milli Fanillis...

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:56.767
or Manilliacs.

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:03.133
This was a joke we had.

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:08.434
Archeologists in Lao --
I said Laos --

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:09.901
recently discovered
an ancient tooth

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:11.868
thought to belong
to an extinct human species

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:13.534
that was lodged in a cave wall.

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:17.334
Experts believe their last words
were "not cake."

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:18.834
I then went on --
joke was written fine.

00:04:18.834 --> 00:04:20.501
I then went on
and explained the joke

00:04:20.501 --> 00:04:23.501
and said he thought the wall
was cake.

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:25.868
I did not realize,
and shame on me,

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:29.400
it was a female skull tooth --

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.968
I guess the tooth, and then
they work their way back.

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:35.701
Tooth, skull, body,
and then they know.

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:38.467
But shame on me
for assuming it was a man.

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:42.167
Women can also bite a wall,
thinking it's cake.

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:46.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.267
Someone else said
that joke doesn't work

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:49.968
because cake
hadn't been invented yet.

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:55.234
Is that an invention --
cake?

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:58.434
Maybe go to @seacaptainpolls.
Maybe we'll put that up there.

00:04:58.434 --> 00:05:01.400
Do you think cake
is an invention?

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:05.300
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.501
Cake hadn't been invented yet.

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:08.501
That's why people
were biting wall --

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:09.834
They were so desperate for --

00:05:09.834 --> 00:05:11.434
That's how they were trying
to go about finding out

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:13.434
if it had been invented.

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:14.868
They were just biting
everything.

00:05:17.234 --> 00:05:19.067
Kimmel -- oh, boy.

00:05:19.067 --> 00:05:21.067
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:26.300
Jimmy Kimmel last week --
you know, he got COVID.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.467
He went on his show
after he got better,

00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:31.400
called me out by name,

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.567
saying that of all
the talk-show hosts,

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:35.033
I hadn't reached out.

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:38.100
I apologized.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.033
To make up for it,
I sent him here --

00:05:40.033 --> 00:05:45.133
You watched me put the soup
in a FedEx box to send him.

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:48.133
Then he got COVID again.

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:50.334
And, obviously,
I didn't want him to have COVID,

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:53.567
but pretty catbird seat of me,

00:05:53.567 --> 00:05:55.667
'cause my soup's
already en route.

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:57.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.801 --> 00:05:59.767
My make-up soup
is gonna arrive --

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:02.734
It's like no one's gonna beat
my new soup.

00:06:02.734 --> 00:06:04.567
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:08.100
Obviously, perfect world,
he doesn't get COVID at all.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:11.534
Second place is how
it's laid out for me.

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:19.000
Speaking of Kimmel -- and this
is why I'm a little irked --

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:22.634
Dear friend Jimmy Kimmel,
get well soon.

00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:25.767
Can't host the show
'cause he got COVID again.

00:06:25.767 --> 00:06:28.534
So who fills in for him
last night?

00:06:28.534 --> 00:06:33.133
Sandberg --
Mulaney and Sandberg.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:36.033
So when I call Sandberg,
nothing, no answer.

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:40.934
Kimmel calls,
"Hello, Mr. Kimmel."

00:06:40.934 --> 00:06:43.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.367
"What do you need, Mr. Kimmel?
Right away, Mr. Kimmel."

00:06:45.367 --> 00:06:48.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.701
I'm not gonna call Sandberg
anymore.

00:06:52.701 --> 00:06:55.767
I'm taking that out
of this equation.

00:06:55.767 --> 00:07:01.067
I will just write him now,
see if he's available.

00:07:01.067 --> 00:07:02.667
And we will see
if he writes back.

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:07.567
But, I mean, really,
pretty heartbreaking that --

00:07:07.567 --> 00:07:10.234
I mean, it's almost like the way
the fact that he did Kimmel

00:07:10.234 --> 00:07:12.000
and he's not showing up
for this,

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.367
it's almost like he's valuing
an 11:30 network talk show

00:07:16.367 --> 00:07:18.234
more than "Corrections."

00:07:18.234 --> 00:07:23.901
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.901 --> 00:07:25.300
I said if Trump wrote a book,

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:27.400
he would be the first person
in history

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:30.367
to write one
without ever reading one.

00:07:30.367 --> 00:07:34.934
A very clever little jackal
pointed out at minimum,

00:07:34.934 --> 00:07:36.734
he would be the second person
that would be true of,

00:07:36.734 --> 00:07:37.901
because it would also be true

00:07:37.901 --> 00:07:40.567
of the first person
who ever wrote a book.

00:07:40.567 --> 00:07:43.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:45.000
And there's a lot of answers
to this,

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.400
as nobody knows for sure
what the first book was.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.767
So don't jackal me on this,
okay,

00:07:50.767 --> 00:07:53.634
'cause there are some things
we can't know.

00:07:53.634 --> 00:07:57.234
But based on what I did
research wise,

00:07:57.234 --> 00:08:02.567
it was "Epic of Gilgamesh"
by James Patterson.

00:08:02.567 --> 00:08:06.667
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.667 --> 00:08:08.701
Not that one.

00:08:08.701 --> 00:08:10.300
It was his dad.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.033
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:12.033 --> 00:08:15.934
It was cool, he had the idea
to write a book

00:08:15.934 --> 00:08:18.534
when he was at the airport
and he saw Hudson Booksellers.

00:08:18.534 --> 00:08:26.234
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:26.234 --> 00:08:29.501
Pizza Hut sent this hat.

00:08:29.501 --> 00:08:31.000
There we go.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.434
We had kind of mocked this up,

00:08:32.434 --> 00:08:34.267
and then they actually
had it made.

00:08:39.033 --> 00:08:40.567
Pizza Hut must have --

00:08:40.567 --> 00:08:43.567
'cause Pizza Hut
is coming on to us pretty hard.

00:08:43.567 --> 00:08:45.968
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:45.968 --> 00:08:47.434
Pizza Hut must have --
[ Cellphone chimes ]

00:08:51.534 --> 00:08:53.901
[ Sighs ] Sorry.

00:08:53.901 --> 00:08:56.767
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.767 --> 00:09:01.133
"Are you available?"
Right now?

00:09:01.133 --> 00:09:04.167
"Are you in the middle of it?"
Yeah.

00:09:04.167 --> 00:09:05.634
[bleep]

00:09:05.634 --> 00:09:08.167
[ Laughter ]

00:09:08.167 --> 00:09:10.033
[ Cellphone chimes ]

00:09:10.033 --> 00:09:11.033
Alright.

00:09:11.033 --> 00:09:13.033
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:18.968 --> 00:09:21.801
I got to scroll back a long time
to the last time we talked.

00:09:21.801 --> 00:09:25.868
[ Cellphone ringing ]

00:09:25.868 --> 00:09:29.334
[ Speaks indistinctly ]

00:09:29.334 --> 00:09:31.834
Hey, what's up, dude?
-What's up, man?

00:09:31.834 --> 00:09:35.400
-What did you do last night?
-Oh, I just hosted "Kimmel."

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.033
-[ Chuckles ]

00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:38.400
Yeah, everybody here
is pretty bummed out

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:41.033
that you would do that
and not hang out with us.

00:09:41.033 --> 00:09:43.000
-Well, you're in New York
is the problem,

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.968
why I go there.

00:09:44.968 --> 00:09:47.400
-Hey, I've been trying to talk
to you for, like, five weeks

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.734
'cause Nic Cage
wanted you to host "SNL" as him.

00:09:50.734 --> 00:09:52.667
-Uh-huh.
-Would you have done that?

00:09:52.667 --> 00:09:55.901
-In a heartbeat.
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:55.901 --> 00:09:56.968
-Okay, so, I've thought a lot

00:09:56.968 --> 00:09:59.167
about what I would write
if that happened,

00:09:59.167 --> 00:10:00.868
and I want to give you
the presence --

00:10:00.868 --> 00:10:04.334
the premise and the first line,
and I want you to just start.

00:10:04.334 --> 00:10:05.467
-Okay.
-Okay.

00:10:05.467 --> 00:10:08.734
You as Nic Cage walk out
to do the monologue,

00:10:08.734 --> 00:10:11.067
but the premise
is you are John Travolta

00:10:11.067 --> 00:10:12.667
wearing a Nic Cage face.

00:10:12.667 --> 00:10:16.234
[ Laughter ]

00:10:16.234 --> 00:10:19.767
And the first line of the
monologue is "Stop clapping!"

00:10:19.767 --> 00:10:24.501
[ Laughter ]

00:10:24.501 --> 00:10:26.234
-[ As Nic Cage ] Stop clapping!

00:10:26.234 --> 00:10:27.968
I'm not Castor Troy!

00:10:27.968 --> 00:10:30.200
[ Laughter ]

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.267
You don't understand!

00:10:31.267 --> 00:10:33.467
There's been
a big miscommunication!

00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:35.534
He's sleeping with my wife!

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:38.234
[ Laughter ]

00:10:38.234 --> 00:10:40.701
Lord!
Lord, you got to believe me!

00:10:40.701 --> 00:10:44.200
[ Laughter ]

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:46.300
-Did you like hosting
a talk show?

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:48.968
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:48.968 --> 00:10:50.334
-You look really good, though.

00:10:50.334 --> 00:10:52.200
I feel like the fact that
you did a talk show last night,

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.501
this is the best
you've ever looked on FaceTime.

00:10:54.501 --> 00:10:57.567
-Well, I shaved my face.

00:10:57.567 --> 00:11:00.200
Like, having to prep
for a guest,

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:02.868
like, it's like being trapped
hosting a dinner party.

00:11:02.868 --> 00:11:04.534
-Yeah, I know all this.
Okay, bye.

00:11:04.534 --> 00:11:06.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:06.434 --> 00:11:07.667
I hosted one.

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:10.968
[ Laughter ]

00:11:10.968 --> 00:11:12.067
Why would he tell me?

00:11:12.067 --> 00:11:13.734
Literally,
it's what I do for a living.

00:11:13.734 --> 00:11:19.300
[ Laughter ]

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:22.300
[ Chuckling ]

00:11:29.367 --> 00:11:31.534
Where was I?
Pizza Hut's coming on to us.

00:11:31.534 --> 00:11:33.234
[ Laughter ]

00:11:33.234 --> 00:11:34.834
Pizza Hut --

00:11:34.834 --> 00:11:36.834
[ Chuckling ]

00:11:36.834 --> 00:11:39.234
Pizza -- [ Laughs ]

00:11:39.234 --> 00:11:42.133
Alright, hold on.

00:11:42.133 --> 00:11:44.868
I feel like the timing of that
was really inopportune,

00:11:44.868 --> 00:11:49.767
because I feel like this joke
would have worked better.

00:11:49.767 --> 00:11:51.400
I'm gonna pretend like
it didn't happen.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:54.567
Shoot, Pizza Hut must have eaten
some of their pizza,

00:11:54.567 --> 00:11:56.234
because, uh, they're thirsty.

00:11:56.234 --> 00:12:00.267
[ Laughter ]

00:12:00.267 --> 00:12:03.901
Pizza Hut is not a sponsor
of "Corrections."

00:12:03.901 --> 00:12:05.334
I want to make that clear.

00:12:05.334 --> 00:12:07.834
One day, they might be, however.

00:12:07.834 --> 00:12:10.300
They obviously
watch "Corrections."

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.267
We appreciate the engagement.

00:12:12.267 --> 00:12:15.067
Again,
pizza hats is the only product

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:17.200
that we're promoting today.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.601
You can go to pizzahats.com,
I think.

00:12:19.601 --> 00:12:21.534
I can't remember
if we bought that domain name.

00:12:21.534 --> 00:12:22.968
I feel like we did.

00:12:22.968 --> 00:12:24.834
Anyway,
Pizza Hut is not a sponsor.

00:12:24.834 --> 00:12:27.467
But if they are
and all of a sudden,

00:12:27.467 --> 00:12:31.801
you know, "Corrections" starts
"Brought to you by Pizza Hut,"

00:12:31.801 --> 00:12:32.968
if all of you start saying,

00:12:32.968 --> 00:12:35.534
"Oh, my God,
I can't believe you sold out,"

00:12:35.534 --> 00:12:39.801
I want you to know that is
exactly what we will have done.

00:12:39.801 --> 00:12:41.801
[ Laughter ]

00:12:45.467 --> 00:12:46.901
Pizza Hut is in the mix.

00:12:46.901 --> 00:12:51.267
We have another very exciting
product in the mix as a sponsor.

00:12:51.267 --> 00:12:53.200
We talked about Vathers --

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:57.467
Werther's Originals.

00:12:57.467 --> 00:12:58.501
This is so exciting.

00:12:58.501 --> 00:12:59.501
We didn't even know
it was a product,

00:12:59.501 --> 00:13:01.934
but they reached out.

00:13:01.934 --> 00:13:09.033
It's a new candy by one of
our favorite directors here,

00:13:09.033 --> 00:13:11.100
Werner's Originals.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:14.434
[ Light laughter ]

00:13:14.434 --> 00:13:20.701
Werner's Originals hard candy
is a delicious butterscotch,

00:13:20.701 --> 00:13:25.234
the center of which
is a gaping void.

00:13:25.234 --> 00:13:28.467
[ Light laughter ]

00:13:28.467 --> 00:13:34.834
Werner's Originals,
because life sucks.

00:13:34.834 --> 00:13:38.167
[ Light laughter ]

00:13:38.167 --> 00:13:43.100
I feel like we maybe
just stumbled into a desk piece,

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:45.734
like sponsors
who aren't so great.

00:13:45.734 --> 00:13:48.734
[ Laughter ]

00:13:51.567 --> 00:13:53.534
Put a pin in it, Shoemaker.

00:13:55.767 --> 00:13:58.267
Trump, we said,

00:13:58.267 --> 00:14:00.734
he would have shot
Patriot missiles at Mexico.

00:14:00.734 --> 00:14:02.634
Patriot missiles or anti-air.

00:14:02.634 --> 00:14:04.634
Tomahawk missiles
would have been better.

00:14:04.634 --> 00:14:06.767
We also said jokingly

00:14:06.767 --> 00:14:10.701
that Mexico would obviously know
it was America.

00:14:10.701 --> 00:14:14.934
And then we had a line

00:14:14.934 --> 00:14:16.868
of Mexico thinking
maybe it was Costa Rica.

00:14:16.868 --> 00:14:19.534
I'm very happy to say we have
a lot of Costa Rican viewers,

00:14:19.534 --> 00:14:20.801
each of whom told me

00:14:20.801 --> 00:14:23.467
that Costa Rica
has not had an army since 1948.

00:14:23.467 --> 00:14:24.868
And let me just say,

00:14:24.868 --> 00:14:27.234
I don't think it's a mistake
that you don't have an army.

00:14:27.234 --> 00:14:30.334
I think it's a mistake
that you've told us.

00:14:30.334 --> 00:14:33.334
[ Laughter ]

00:14:37.133 --> 00:14:39.701
We're a go on Costa Rica.

00:14:39.701 --> 00:14:43.467
[ Laughter ]

00:14:43.467 --> 00:14:49.200
I earpods.
It's either AirPods or earbuds.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:52.000
It's never earpods.
It's never airbuds.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:54.133
"Air Bud," of course,
was a movie

00:14:54.133 --> 00:14:56.234
about a dog
who could play basketball.

00:14:56.234 --> 00:14:57.901
And I was reading up
about it today.

00:14:57.901 --> 00:14:59.267
This is really cool.

00:14:59.267 --> 00:15:03.234
First movie written solely
so late-night comedy writers

00:15:03.234 --> 00:15:05.634
would have something to
reference for the next 25 years.

00:15:05.634 --> 00:15:07.634
[ Laughter ]

00:15:10.901 --> 00:15:12.400
We're talking about
Madison Cawthorn

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:16.000
and said,
"Every rose has its Cawthorn."

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.100
Some botanists engaged with us.

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:22.234
Roses do not have thorns.
They have prickles.

00:15:22.234 --> 00:15:24.868
There are three different
classifications of sharp points.

00:15:24.868 --> 00:15:26.968
Thorns are modified branches.

00:15:26.968 --> 00:15:29.467
Spines are modified
leaf structures.

00:15:29.467 --> 00:15:32.734
Prickles have
no vascular material

00:15:32.734 --> 00:15:35.000
and are easier to remove.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:39.901
So from now on,
don't say thorns, say prickles.

00:15:39.901 --> 00:15:42.834
Tough news for the band Poison.

00:15:42.834 --> 00:15:45.300
[ Light laughter ]

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:46.467
Not that tough.

00:15:46.467 --> 00:15:49.901
"Thorn" already doesn't rhyme
with "dawn."

00:15:49.901 --> 00:15:51.868
[ Laughter ]

00:15:51.868 --> 00:15:53.434
So they're already
halfway there,

00:15:53.434 --> 00:15:55.067
if they want to go
with "prickles."

00:15:55.067 --> 00:15:58.200
[ Light laughter ]

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:00.400
Hey, this was some confusion,
'cause we made a joke

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:01.667
'cause, you know,
Madison Cawthorn

00:16:01.667 --> 00:16:03.701
both talked about
getting invited to orgies

00:16:03.701 --> 00:16:07.434
by members of the GOP
and also mentioned

00:16:07.434 --> 00:16:10.834
the GOP doing cocaine
and offering him a key bump.

00:16:10.834 --> 00:16:14.167
We showed a photograph --
not real --

00:16:14.167 --> 00:16:16.000
of Chuck Grassley
with a bowl of keys,

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.834
inviting the membership
to a key party,

00:16:17.834 --> 00:16:20.300
and some of you thought
we misunderstood

00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:21.334
what a key bump was.

00:16:21.334 --> 00:16:22.601
We know what a key bump is.

00:16:22.601 --> 00:16:26.300
A key bump is when you do
cocaine off a key,

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:27.767
and a key party
is when you throw

00:16:27.767 --> 00:16:29.834
all of the keys in the bowl,
and you pick one out,

00:16:29.834 --> 00:16:31.234
and that's your special friend
for the night.

00:16:31.234 --> 00:16:32.634
I just think
the important thing to remember

00:16:32.634 --> 00:16:34.567
is in the modern GOP,
when you see a key,

00:16:34.567 --> 00:16:37.133
the only thing you know for
certain is it ain't for doors.

00:16:37.133 --> 00:16:40.133
[ Laughter ]

00:16:42.133 --> 00:16:49.834
So, last night's "Closer Look,"
we goofed on...

00:16:49.834 --> 00:16:54.300
I guess you could say
Italian-American stereotypes.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:59.000
Someone reached out
and said it was lazy.

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:00.200
Which breaks my heart,

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:03.701
because I then obviously
take this to heart.

00:17:03.701 --> 00:17:09.567
And so I went to the office
of "Closer Look's" head writer,

00:17:09.567 --> 00:17:11.634
[ Italian accent ]
Salvatore Gentile.

00:17:11.634 --> 00:17:14.868
[ Laughter ]

00:17:14.868 --> 00:17:15.868
[ Normal voice ]
And, you know, post show,

00:17:15.868 --> 00:17:17.133
he does not like
to be bothered.

00:17:17.133 --> 00:17:20.467
He was eating his prosciutt...

00:17:20.467 --> 00:17:24.567
[ Laughter ]

00:17:24.567 --> 00:17:27.200
...dumping his biscott
in his capucchuch.

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:30.601
[ Laughter ]

00:17:30.601 --> 00:17:33.100
Tiny, tiny little napkin.

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:34.634
It almost defeats the purpose,

00:17:34.634 --> 00:17:37.667
'cause it covers so little
of the shirt, little napkin.

00:17:37.667 --> 00:17:39.934
And he was like,
"Whosah this?"

00:17:39.934 --> 00:17:41.334
[ Laughter ]

00:17:41.334 --> 00:17:46.100
"Whosah this about a..."

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:47.400
Anyway,
I do think he took it.

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:49.834
I do think he took it
to heart.

00:17:49.834 --> 00:17:54.267
♪ Just like every deli
has its pickles ♪

00:17:54.267 --> 00:17:56.767
[ Light laughter ]

00:17:56.767 --> 00:17:58.367
So that would work.

00:18:00.934 --> 00:18:05.400
We've got three real special
kids who work on this show.

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:08.734
They came to us via a program

00:18:08.734 --> 00:18:13.868
of kids who wanted
to break into the biz.

00:18:13.868 --> 00:18:18.133
And we just try to provide them
sort of in-the-door experience.

00:18:21.033 --> 00:18:23.467
Seth Reiss, Matt Goldich,
and Ben Warheit.

00:18:23.467 --> 00:18:26.234
[ Laughter ]

00:18:26.234 --> 00:18:29.167
And they write "Ya Burnt."
They're the Burn Boys.

00:18:29.167 --> 00:18:31.968
That's how they're known
around the office.

00:18:31.968 --> 00:18:33.501
And "Ya Burnt"
is such a great sketch.

00:18:33.501 --> 00:18:35.434
And the one we did this week
was a lot of fun,

00:18:35.434 --> 00:18:37.467
and there were some new moves
in it.

00:18:37.467 --> 00:18:39.100
And hopefully
you guys enjoyed watching it

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:41.033
as much as I enjoyed doing it.

00:18:41.033 --> 00:18:46.100
Now, unlike "A Closer Look --"
We plan "A Closer Look."

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.601
Each "Closer Look" is planned
a month in advance.

00:18:49.601 --> 00:18:52.367
Whereas...
[ Laughter ]

00:18:52.367 --> 00:18:54.534
"Ya Burnt --" they find out
about "Ya Burnt"

00:18:54.534 --> 00:18:56.200
like an hour before we tape.
[ Laughter ]

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:58.701
So I don't want to be
too hard on them,

00:18:58.701 --> 00:19:03.100
because they're just
pulling elements together.

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:05.467
It's really unfair
what we ask of them.

00:19:05.467 --> 00:19:08.334
[ Laughter ]

00:19:08.334 --> 00:19:11.834
And yet
it was both really funny

00:19:11.834 --> 00:19:14.968
and there were no mistakes,
so I'm pretty psyched.

00:19:14.968 --> 00:19:17.934
I do tip my cap
to the Burn Boys.

00:19:20.367 --> 00:19:23.400
Oh, wait.
[ Laughter ]

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.300
There were a few.

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:27.400
We did a really --

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:30.868
We burned people
who post their Wordle scores.

00:19:30.868 --> 00:19:33.434
That was it right there.
That's what it looked like.

00:19:33.434 --> 00:19:36.501
And immediately you can see
people post it out

00:19:36.501 --> 00:19:38.167
'cause, you know,
we're burning.

00:19:38.167 --> 00:19:41.834
So, that is wrong.

00:19:41.834 --> 00:19:44.100
You wouldn't have two T's
yellow.

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:46.567
That would be gray.

00:19:46.567 --> 00:19:51.367
But not bad,
that one mistake.

00:19:51.367 --> 00:19:53.033
They have an hour
to pull it together.

00:19:53.033 --> 00:19:55.901
Oh, right.
It says right here, "AOL CD's."

00:19:55.901 --> 00:19:58.434
Everybody said,
"Why is that an apostrophe 'S'?"

00:19:58.434 --> 00:19:59.434
That wouldn't be that.

00:19:59.434 --> 00:20:00.901
It wouldn't be a possessive
on "CD."

00:20:00.901 --> 00:20:02.000
So just two.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.534
Oh, it did say
an eight-hour road trip,

00:20:03.534 --> 00:20:04.701
and a sentence later said

00:20:04.701 --> 00:20:07.000
we were stuck in a turnpike
for 10 hours.

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:09.167
This is one person
who pointed out all these.

00:20:09.167 --> 00:20:11.167
[ Laughter ]

00:20:14.634 --> 00:20:17.801
Also, we even talked about it
backstage.

00:20:17.801 --> 00:20:20.367
I said, "We're talking about
Inspector Gadget."

00:20:20.367 --> 00:20:23.434
And I said,
"Is he from the '80s?"

00:20:23.434 --> 00:20:26.934
And one of them --
I won't say his name,

00:20:26.934 --> 00:20:29.100
but I will say
it's the same as mine,

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:32.200
said...
[ Laughter ]

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:35.667
"No, I think Inspector Gadget's
from the from the early '90s,"

00:20:35.667 --> 00:20:37.033
and so that's what I said.

00:20:37.033 --> 00:20:38.701
In their defense --

00:20:38.701 --> 00:20:41.968
In the Burn Boys defense,
none of them have the Internet.

00:20:41.968 --> 00:20:44.701
[ Laughter ]

00:20:44.701 --> 00:20:48.234
So everything is a series of,
like, instincts plus guesses.

00:20:48.234 --> 00:20:51.167
[ Laughter ]

00:20:51.167 --> 00:20:52.801
They're very anti-technology.

00:20:52.801 --> 00:20:56.634
They're like the Amish
without the work ethic.

00:20:56.634 --> 00:21:01.968
[ Laughter ]

00:21:01.968 --> 00:21:07.834
But we -- This is real.

00:21:07.834 --> 00:21:09.634
This one killed me,
'cause, you know, I read.

00:21:09.634 --> 00:21:12.267
Obviously,
I go through these, right?

00:21:12.267 --> 00:21:13.701
You know that now.

00:21:13.701 --> 00:21:15.567
I go through
all your corrections,

00:21:15.567 --> 00:21:17.901
and there's no gatekeeping.

00:21:17.901 --> 00:21:19.901
If you leave a correction,
I'm gonna read it.

00:21:19.901 --> 00:21:22.868
So...

00:21:22.868 --> 00:21:27.434
We had a joke about Jason
from "Friday the 13th"

00:21:27.434 --> 00:21:29.501
waiting for night to fall

00:21:29.501 --> 00:21:34.667
so that he could kill
his victims.

00:21:34.667 --> 00:21:39.300
So, this was a comment I got
in the comments section.

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:43.334
"Hey. It's Scollins."
[ Light laughter ]

00:21:43.334 --> 00:21:45.601
"This is my first-ever
YouTube comment.

00:21:45.601 --> 00:21:47.567
Jason very often kills
during the day,

00:21:47.567 --> 00:21:48.834
so I don't know if it's right

00:21:48.834 --> 00:21:51.100
to say he's waiting
for night to fall.

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:53.367
Maybe you're thinking
of Dracula."

00:21:53.367 --> 00:21:55.167
[ Laughter ]

00:21:55.167 --> 00:21:56.534
And it breaks my heart,

00:21:56.534 --> 00:21:59.067
because I have really gone
out of my way

00:21:59.067 --> 00:22:00.934
to Scollins-proof my life.

00:22:00.934 --> 00:22:04.901
[ Laughter ]

00:22:04.901 --> 00:22:07.701
And for him
to just sneak in like that is --

00:22:07.701 --> 00:22:09.367
Well, he got me.

00:22:09.367 --> 00:22:14.400
But I do want to thank
all my writers, you know?

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:19.033
All jokes aside,
everything I said is true.

00:22:19.033 --> 00:22:24.968
And I think we are done.

